# Rite of Replication ({2}{U}{U}, kicker {5}): "Create a token that's a copy of target creature." Bot2 has a Llanowar Elves and a
# Forest; the Forest is no creature, so it is refused as a target (CR 115.1) beside the Elves, which are copied (CR 707.2).
# Cast without the kicker it makes exactly one token, under Bot1's control, which has the Elves' mana ability and is a token
# (CR 111.1); Bot2's own Elves are untouched. Paid by a Black Lotus and a Mox Jet.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Rite of Replication
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Hand.Rite of Replication.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Forest)
Bot1.Hand.Rite of Replication.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Llanowar Elves
[Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Token = true
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Emerald; Forest; Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Graveyard = Rite of Replication; Black Lotus
Stack.Count = 0
